## Third-party marks

tapkey displays the marks of the coding tools and API providers it works with, so that
you can recognise them at a glance. Those marks belong to their respective owners:

- Claude and the Anthropic mark are trademarks of Anthropic PBC
- OpenAI and the OpenAI mark are trademarks of OpenAI, Inc.
- OpenCode is a trademark of Anomaly Innovations, Inc.
- DeepSeek, OpenRouter, Ollama, Qwen, Z.ai, Moonshot and any other provider or tool
  marks are trademarks of their respective owners

Marks are rendered monochrome, at a single optical weight, purely to identify the tool or
provider a row refers to. tapkey is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any
of these companies, and no mark is used to suggest otherwise.

### Where each outline comes from

Marks are traced from the owner's own current asset wherever one is published, not from an
aggregator, because aggregators lag: at the time of writing Simple Icons carried a
superseded OpenRouter mark, a pre-2025 OpenAI mark, and stale brand colours for two others.

- OpenAI — the Blossom as refreshed in February 2025
- OpenRouter — the "OR" monogram introduced 13 July 2026, from the vendor's own
  `/brand/v2/` assets; the earlier routing glyph is retired
- OpenCode — `packages/identity/mark.svg` from the project's own repository, normalised
  from 512 to 24 units; its second tone is carried as reduced opacity rather than dropped
- Z.ai — the glyph from the vendor's own logo asset, cropped out of its dark plate
- Claude, DeepSeek, Ollama, Qwen — Simple Icons outlines, each verified against the
  owner's live asset

Simple Icons is CC0-1.0. The CC0 dedication covers the icon files, not the trademarks
they depict.

### Removal

Several of these owners publish trademark guidelines that ask for prior written
permission before their logo is displayed by a third party, and some ask that their mark
not be altered, including recolouring. tapkey shows them monochrome under a nominative-use
reading: the mark identifies the tool a row acts on and nothing more.

If you own one of these marks and would like its use here changed or removed, open an
issue, or write to the address in the repository metadata, and it will be removed in the
next release — no discussion required.
